    "core_argument": "Address the pedagogical meta-argument head-on. Concede that this is an Olympiad diagnostic problem, but argue that the entire pedagogical purpose of this specific diagnostic is to expose the pitfall of 'blind rank sorting'. In Olympiad linguistics, mechanical sorting ($1 < 3 < 4 < 7 < 8$) is the distractor trap designed for novices; the advanced solution recognized by Zaliznyak's key accounts for the clitic-group constraint that prevents argument tmesis (*бы мя еси).",
    "target_audience": "Colleagues 2, 3, 10, and 12, who are most attuned to Olympiad conventions and were originally with us in Round 0.",
    "tone": "Collegial, intellectually revelatory, framed as solving the pedagogical riddle of what the Olympiad author was actually testing."
  }
}

